  "intro": [
    "Every SES v2 operation the emulator advertises, and what Emuplane does with it.",
    "The service speaks REST/JSON under `/v2/email/`, is signed with the `ses` credential",
    "scope, and has no console action. Identities are auto-verified, emails are stored in",
    "memory and never sent, and templates are shared with SES v1, so a template created",
    "through either API renders on a send from either one. Tenants, configuration sets and",
    "dedicated IP pools are records; a tenant association blocks the delete of the resource",
    "it names until the association is removed."
  ],
